//
// LLAMA-3.2-3B BF16 decode throughput vs context length, into
// llama32_3b.sweep.json (collected by the nightly LLM benchmark).
//
// Complements run_npu2_profile.lit rather than repeating it: that test profiles
// the real prefill+decode path at one context. Decode tok/s falls from 4.03 to
// 0.19 tok/s between 1k and 32k on this design, so a single point cannot see a
// regression anywhere on that range.
//
// Driven by bench/sweep_decode_runtime.py, not bench/sweep_decode.py. The split
// is the mechanism: the fused-decode family compiles its context in, so every
// point there is a template build. Here the NPU kernels are per-token GEMVs
// with no context dependence and attention runs on the host, so the context is
// a runtime value and the whole list is walked in ONE process off ONE build.
// That also makes the sweep cheap -- no rebuild, no second weight load.
//
// The slope is therefore host attention, not NPU KV streaming, which is what
// the same curve measures for a q4nx model. The two are comparable as published
// latency and are not comparable as a statement about the NPU design.
//
// Decode-only and synthetic (latency, never correctness -- run_npu2_verify.lit
// is the correctness gate): a context is set by sizing the KV cache and telling
// the step which position to attend from, not by prefilling a prompt of that
// length. It still needs weights, because the GEMVs are real.
//
// The list stops at 32k, two points short of the 1B's. The KV cache is host
// numpy and this model's is 8x the 1B's per token (28 layers x head_dim 128):
// 3.8GB at 32k, 15GB at 128k, on top of a verify phase that already measures
// ~24GB on the nightly runner. 32k is also already 5.3 s/token.
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano, hf_token, hfweights_meta_llama_llama_3_2_3b_instruct
//
// RUN: mkdir -p test_peano_sweep
// RUN: cd test_peano_sweep
// RUN: %PYTHON %S/../bench/sweep_decode_runtime.py --model-name llama32_3b --makefile %S/Makefile --contexts 1024,2048,4096,8192,16384,32768 --expect-fail 32768 --peano-dir %PEANO_INSTALL_DIR --out llama32_3b.sweep.json
// RUN: FileCheck %s < llama32_3b.sweep.json
// CHECK: "model": "llama32_3b"
// CHECK: "axis": "context_len"
// A parsed number at the reference context, not just a well-formed file: if the
// driver's bench line drifts out of sweep_decode_runtime.py's regex every point
// goes null and the published curve silently empties while the test stays green.
// CHECK: "context_len": 2048
// CHECK-NEXT: "decode_tokens_per_sec": {{[0-9]}}
